"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in v4.7.dev1.official [bf95b6258]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.dev1 - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated Intel(R) Iris(R) Xe Graphics (Intel Corporation; 32.0.101.6737) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-1255U (12 threads) - 15.82 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWith #105701 the visual shader editor was extended with shader type texture_blit. \nFor this shader type up to 4 source textures can be added using the `Input` node.\nWhen selecting the first texture (in node editor shown as \"source_texture\") the resulting shader code also contains `source_texture` as an identifier. For shader code this identifier is not defined and `source_texture0` is used instead.\nThe input node seems to output compilable code for all other `source_texture*` parameters available. \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nThe included project contains a single visual shader resource (new_shader.tres) in mode \"TextureBlit\" that simply reads from the `source_texture` input at the current `uv` using the `Texture2D` shader node. The output is routed to `Color0` of the `Output` node. Opening the shader code using `Show generated shader code.` shows the error in the screenshot below.\n\n<img width=\"559\" height=\"97\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c78148b1-ab02-45b5-8752-0fd31a050a3d\" />\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[project.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25715927/project.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url"